## Feasibility notes (raid 2026-06-12)

Verified against origin/main b8f054e1. Plan adjustments, exit criteria unchanged:

- `\section*{Related Work — Methods}` (terminator in
  test_manuscript_cohort_and_caveats.py ~L284) has NO label — the helper
  cannot key on it. Slice to the next sectioning command of any kind
  (`\section`, `\section*`, `\appendix`, `\end{document}`), so unlabelled
  terminators work for free.
- The editorial-brief entry named `novelty-conjunction-claim` in this ticket
  is actually slugged `novelty-provenance-temporality` (brief L132).
- Action-5 sweep must also catch `tests/test_manuscript_framing_0513.py:30-31`
  (Introduction→Related Work Empirical title-anchored slice).
- `tests/test_manuscript_exp2_equalization.py::_section6` start is already
  label-keyed; only its terminator (full title of §7) needs the helper.
- `test_manuscript_0512_structure.py` has no extraction to re-key (direct
  string presence checks) — leave the file untouched here.
- `test_manuscript_structure.py:101,108,119` heading presence checks ARE the
  assertion target — stay as-is per the exception rule.
- All target labels confirmed present in main.tex (sec:fusion L821,
  sec:discussion L854, sec:annex-exp2 L1946).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] All manuscript section/annex extraction in tests goes through the
  label-keyed helper
- [ ] Reordering or retitling sections (labels kept) cannot break any
  adherence test except intentional decision pins
- [ ] `make check` passes
